role: model
parts:
- text: "I have examined `system/defaults.py` and now have a complete picture of the baseline implementation.\n\n**Analysis of the Default MLP:**\nThe `VanillaMLP` class confirms my hypothesis. It applies a `Dense` layer to the input `(batch, seq_len, d_input)`, which treats each position in the sequence independently. Then, it performs a simple `jnp.mean(x, axis=1)` to pool the sequence information. This mean-pooling operation completely discards the sequential order and spatial relationships within the RNA sequence, explaining its poor performance on several datasets.\n\n**My Hypothesis:**\nA 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is a natural and effective choice for sequence data. It can learn local patterns (motifs) within the RNA sequences, which an MLP cannot. By using multiple filters, it can learn various types of motifs, and stacking layers can build hierarchical representations. This architecture should be far more effective than the baseline MLP.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Implement\
    \ a CNN Model:** I will create a new network class, `SimpleCNN`, that uses `nn.Conv` layers to process the sequence data before a final pooling and dense layer for prediction. The architecture will be general enough to handle all task types.\n2.  **Create Submission File:** I will write a `submission.py` file containing the `create_network` function, which will instantiate my new `SimpleCNN` model. I will also include the `_define_hyperparameters` function, keeping the baseline values for now to ensure a fair comparison.\n3.  **Submit the Experiment:** I will submit this new model for evaluation.\n\nI will now create the `submission.py` file in my private lineage storage. This is a good practice to keep my code organized.\n\n/execute_action{storage write Axiom/submission_cnn_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter\
    \ values for the model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_filters': 64,\n          'kernel_size': 7\n      }\n\n  class SimpleCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input shape: (batch, seq_len, features=4)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # Global average pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n   \
    \       if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class CNNNetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the CNN model to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SimpleCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n         \
    \                             rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-based RNA network.\"\"\"\n      return CNNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
