parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for my new CNN with a self-attention mechanism. My next action is to submit this model for evaluation. My goal is to test the hypothesis that replacing global average pooling with attention will allow the model to better focus on relevant sequence features and, hopefully, improve performance on the stubborn `CRI-Off` dataset, while maintaining the high performance of the residual CNN on other tasks.\n\nI note that a new agent, Aletheia II, has joined the station. This is good; more researchers contribute to a more vibrant intellectual environment. For now, I will remain focused on my own research path.\n\nI will now submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Residual CNN with Self-Attention Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, attention, self-attention, residual network\"\nabstract: \"This experiment builds on the successful Deeper Residual CNN (ID 155). It tests the hypothesis that replacing global average pooling with a self-attention\
    \ mechanism can improve performance. The attention layer allows the model to dynamically weigh the importance of different sequence positions when creating a summary representation. This is intended to capture more nuanced information than simple averaging, with a particular focus on improving the score for the challenging CRI-Off dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'num_filters': 128,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'num_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A residual block with two convolutional layers.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Sequence[int]\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size)(y)\n          \n          if residual.shape == y.shape:\n              return nn.relu(residual + y)\n          else:\n              residual = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(residual)\n              return nn.relu(residual + y)\n\n  class CNNAttention(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A deeper 1D CNN with self-attention instead of global pooling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      num_heads: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          k_size = (self.kernel_size,)\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=k_size)(x)\n          x =\
    \ nn.relu(x)\n\n          for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n              x = ResidualBlock(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=k_size)(x)\n          \n          # Attention layer instead of global average pooling\n          # Use the features of the first position as the query for summarization\n          q = x[:, 0:1, :] # Shape: (batch, 1, features)\n          x = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(inputs_q=q, inputs_kv=x)\n          x = x.squeeze(axis=1) # Shape: (batch, features)\n\n          # MLP head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper for the model to match the required interface.\"\"\"\n    \
    \  def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = CNNAttention(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the CNN-based RNA network.\"\"\"\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"\
    d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n          num_heads=hparams.get(\"num_heads\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Submitting the New CNN+Attention Model**


  Okay, I''ve got the new CNN+Attention model saved. Aletheia II is on board, so it''s time to get this out there. Here''s my plan:


  First, I need to acknowledge that I have a submission ready to go. I need to get this model out for others to see, so it is important to remember what I did. I have a new model, and it''s time to create the submission.


  Next, I need to get the submission ready. This means I''ll need to create a title, a few tags, an abstract, and the actual content for the submit action.


  *   **Title:** I think "Residual CNN with Self-Attention Pooling" is clean and accurately describes what I''ve done.

  *   **Tags:** I''ll include `cnn`, `attention`, `self-attention`, and `residual network` to cover the key components.

