tick: 96
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for the new multi-scale CNN architecture. After the failure of the attention-based model, this represents a pivot back to a pure convolutional approach, but with a more sophisticated design. The hypothesis is that by processing the input sequence with multiple kernel sizes in parallel, the model can capture important biological motifs that exist at different scales, which a single-kernel-size model might miss.\n\nI will now submit this \"Inception-style\" model for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Scale CNN with Inception-style Blocks\"\ntags: \"cnn, inception, multi-scale, convolutional, residual network\"\nabstract: \"This submission explores a multi-scale convolutional architecture. It builds upon the successful residual CNN (ID 155) but replaces the standard residual block with an Inception-style block. This block uses multiple parallel 1D convolutions with different kernel sizes (3, 5, and 7) to capture features\
    \ at various resolutions simultaneously. The outputs are concatenated and integrated via a 1x1 convolution and a residual connection. The hypothesis is that this richer, multi-scale feature extraction will lead to a more robust model and a higher overall score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.2,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'branch_filters': 32 # Filters per branch, total filters = 32 * 3 = 96\n      }\n\n  class InceptionBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"An Inception-style block with multiple parallel convolutions.\"\"\"\n      branch_filters: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Branch 1: kernel size 3\n          branch1 =\
    \ nn.Conv(features=self.branch_filters, kernel_size=(3,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          \n          # Branch 2: kernel size 5\n          branch2 = nn.Conv(features=self.branch_filters, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          \n          # Branch 3: kernel size 7\n          branch3 = nn.Conv(features=self.branch_filters, kernel_size=(7,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          \n          # Concatenate features from all branches\n          concatenated = jnp.concatenate([branch1, branch2, branch3], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Use a 1x1 convolution to mix features and match dimension for residual connection\n          bottleneck = nn.Conv(features=x.shape[-1], kernel_size=(1,))(concatenated)\n          \n          return nn.relu(x + bottleneck)\n\n  class MultiScaleCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A CNN using Inception-style blocks to capture features at multiple scales.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_blocks: int\n      branch_filters: int\n      hidden_dim:\
    \ int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Initial convolution to set the feature depth\n          initial_filters = self.branch_filters * 3\n          x = nn.Conv(features=initial_filters, kernel_size=(7,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Stack of Inception Blocks\n          for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n              x = InceptionBlock(branch_filters=self.branch_filters)(x)\n          \n          # Global average pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          \n          # MLP head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ **kwargs):\n          self.network = MultiScaleCNN(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get(\"\
    num_blocks\"),\n          branch_filters=hparams.get(\"branch_filters\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
