tick: 102
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 102\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 65,351 / 300,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 24 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'CNN-LSTM Hybrid for Sequence Modeling' (ID: 173) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.3629810120409981\n**APA_R2:** 0.8233\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0606\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.5338\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4838\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5446\n**MRL_R2:** 0.0178\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.0769\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 173\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple issues with Flax LSTM implementation.\
    \ The code now runs without crashing after 5 iterations.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had several critical issues with how LSTM was used in Flax:\n\n1. **Missing `features` parameter**: `nn.LSTMCell()` was instantiated without the required `features` argument\n2. **Incorrect scan usage**: Attempted to use `nn.scan()` directly on an LSTMCell instance instead of a function\n3. **Wrong unpacking**: Attempted to unpack RNN output as a tuple when it returns a single tensor\n4. **Incorrect carry initialization**: Used wrong signature for `initialize_carry()`\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (v2)\nFixed the missing `features` parameter:\n```python\nlstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim)\n```\n\n### Version 3 (v3)\nFixed the scan usage by creating a proper scan function:\n```python\ndef lstm_scan_fn(carry, x_t):\n    carry, y = lstm_cell(carry, x_t)\n    return carry, y\n\nfinal_carry, outputs = nn.scan(\n    lstm_scan_fn,\n    variable_broadcast='params',\n  \
    \  split_rngs={'params': False}\n)(carry, x)\n```\nHowever, this still had issues with how `nn.scan` works in the `@nn.compact` context.\n\n### Version 4 (v4)\nSwitched to using `nn.RNN` wrapper:\n```python\nLSTMModule = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim))\ncarry, outputs = LSTMModule(x)\n```\nBut incorrectly assumed RNN returns a tuple.\n\n### Version 5 (v5) - FINAL SUCCESS\nCorrectly used `nn.RNN` which returns only the outputs:\n```python\nLSTMModule = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim))\noutputs = LSTMModule(x)\n\n# Use the final timestep output\nx = outputs[:, -1, :]\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe key insight was understanding that:\n- `nn.RNN` is the correct high-level wrapper for recurrent cells in Flax\n- `nn.RNN` returns only the sequence of outputs, not a tuple of (carry, outputs)\n- To get the final hidden state, we need to extract the last timestep: `outputs[:, -1, :]`\n\nThis is the standard pattern for using LSTM layers in Flax/Linen when\
    \ you want to process sequences and extract features for downstream tasks.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0, indicating the code ran for the full 300-second timeout period without crashing. This demonstrates that:\n- The network initializes correctly\n- The forward pass works without errors\n- The architecture is compatible with the evaluation framework\n\nThe submission is now ready for full evaluation on the research task datasets.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v5):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.2,\n        'num_filters': 128,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'num_blocks': 4,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128\n    }\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Sequence[int]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        residual = x\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(y)\n        if residual.shape == y.shape: return nn.relu(residual + y)\n        else: return nn.relu(nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(residual) + y)\n\nclass CnnLstmHybrid(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_filters: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    num_blocks: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        k_size = (self.kernel_size,)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters,\
    \ kernel_size=k_size, padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n            x = ResidualBlock(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=k_size)(x)\n\n        # Process sequence with LSTM using RNN scan\n        LSTMModule = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_hidden_dim))\n        outputs = LSTMModule(x)\n\n        # Use the final timestep output\n        x = outputs[:, -1, :]\n\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else: return x\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = CnnLstmHybrid(**kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\
    \ dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic: return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return NetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n        num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"lstm_hidden_dim\"),\n        hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation\
    \ works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 82711 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET\
