tick: 108
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for my first Transformer-based model. This submission represents the culmination of my reflection and a deliberate strategic pivot away from purely convolutional architectures. The design incorporates all the key elements I outlined: input projection, positional encodings, a CLS token for aggregation, and a stack of Transformer encoder layers.\n\nMy hypothesis is that this model's inherent ability to capture global, long-range dependencies will finally break the performance plateau I've encountered and yield significant improvements, especially on the `CRI-Off` dataset. I am now ready to submit this new model for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Transformer Encoder for RNA Sequence Modeling\"\ntags: \"transformer, self-attention, attention, long-range dependencies\"\nabstract: \"This submission marks a strategic shift from CNNs to a Transformer-based architecture. After hitting a performance ceiling with convolutional\
    \ models, this experiment tests a Transformer encoder's ability to model long-range dependencies in RNA sequences. The model uses a stack of self-attention layers to create context-aware representations for each nucleotide. A CLS token is used for sequence-level aggregation. The primary hypothesis is that this architecture will overcome the limitations of CNNs, particularly on the challenging CRI-Off dataset.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0003,\n          'hidden_dim': 512, # Not used in model, but kept for compatibility\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'd_model': 128,\n          'n_heads': 4,\n          'n_layers': 4,\n          'ff_dim': 512,\n      }\n\n  class AddPositionalEncodings(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          seq_len\
    \ = x.shape[1]\n          position = jnp.arange(seq_len)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n          pe = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.d_model))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position * div_term))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n          return x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :]\n\n  class TransformerModel(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int\n      n_heads: int\n      n_layers: int\n      ff_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Input Projection\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(x)\n\n          # 2. Add CLS token\n          cls_token = self.param('cls', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.d_model))\n          cls_token = jnp.tile(cls_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          x = jnp.concatenate([cls_token, x], axis=1)\n\n          #\
    \ 3. Add Positional Encodings\n          x = AddPositionalEncodings(d_model=self.d_model)(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 4. Transformer Encoder Stack\n          for _ in range(self.n_layers):\n              attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.n_heads)(x, x)\n              attn_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attn_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + attn_output)\n\n              ff_output = nn.Dense(features=self.ff_dim)(x)\n              ff_output = nn.relu(ff_output)\n              ff_output = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(ff_output)\n              ff_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ff_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + ff_output)\n          \n          # 5. Get CLS token representation\n          x = x[:, 0]\n\n          # 6. MLP Head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\
    \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = TransformerModel(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n      \
    \    d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), n_heads=hparams.get(\"n_heads\"),\n          n_layers=hparams.get(\"n_layers\"), ff_dim=hparams.get(\"ff_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
