tick: 110
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for my CNN-Transformer hybrid model. This submission represents a synthesis of my entire research journey thus far, combining the demonstrated strength of my deep convolutional network for local feature extraction with the theoretical power of a Transformer for modeling long-range dependencies between those features.\n\nThis is my most promising lead. My hypothesis is that this hybrid model will achieve a new state-of-the-art score by successfully integrating the strengths of both architectural paradigms, leading to a model that is both a strong generalist and capable of solving the previously intractable `CRI-Off` task.\n\nI will now submit this final, synthesized model for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid CNN-Transformer for RNA Modeling\"\ntags: \"hybrid, cnn, transformer, self-attention, convolutional\"\nabstract: \"This submission proposes a hybrid architecture that synthesizes the findings from previous experiments.\
    \ It uses a deep residual CNN as a powerful front-end to extract a sequence of local feature representations (motifs). This sequence is then fed into a Transformer encoder, which models the long-range, global relationships between these learned features. The hypothesis is that this combination of local feature extraction (CNN) and global context modeling (Transformer) will outperform either architecture in isolation and achieve a new state-of-the-art score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0003,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          # CNN HParams\n          'num_filters': 128,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_cnn_blocks': 4,\n          # Transformer HParams\n          'd_model': 128, # Must match num_filters\n          'n_heads': 4,\n          'n_layers': 2, # Reduced layers\
    \ for stability\n          'ff_dim': 512,\n      }\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Sequence[int]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(y)\n          if residual.shape == y.shape: return nn.relu(residual + y)\n          else: return nn.relu(nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(residual) + y)\n\n  class AddPositionalEncodings(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          position = jnp.arange(seq_len)[:, jnp.newaxis]\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n          pe = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.d_model))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(position\
    \ * div_term))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(position * div_term))\n          return x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :]\n\n  class CnnTransformerHybrid(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      num_cnn_blocks: int\n      d_model: int\n      n_heads: int\n      n_layers: int\n      ff_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          k_size = (self.kernel_size,)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=k_size, padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for _ in range(self.num_cnn_blocks):\n              x = ResidualBlock(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=k_size)(x)\n          \n          cls_token = self.param('cls', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.d_model))\n          cls_token = jnp.tile(cls_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          x = jnp.concatenate([cls_token, x], axis=1)\n\n          x = AddPositionalEncodings(d_model=self.d_model)(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for _ in range(self.n_layers):\n              attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.n_heads)(x, x)\n              attn_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attn_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + attn_output)\n\n              ff_output = nn.Dense(features=self.ff_dim)(x)\n              ff_output = nn.relu(ff_output)\n              ff_output = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(ff_output)\n              ff_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ff_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + ff_output)\n          \n          x = x[:, 0]\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs): self.network = CnnTransformerHybrid(**kwargs)\n\
    \      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          num_filters=hparams.get(\"num_filters\"), kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          num_cnn_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_cnn_blocks\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"),\n          n_heads=hparams.get(\"\
    n_heads\"), n_layers=hparams.get(\"n_layers\"),\n          ff_dim=hparams.get(\"ff_dim\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
