tick: 114
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved the code for my dispatcher model. This is the most sophisticated submission I have designed, as it encapsulates a meta-architectural decision based on the specific task being evaluated. It leverages my powerful generalist model for most datasets while deploying a specialized Siamese network to target the unique structure of the `CRI-Off` problem.\n\nMy hypothesis is that this task-aware approach will allow me to retain the high performance of my hybrid model on six of the datasets, while finally achieving a significant breakthrough on the seventh, `CRI-Off`, leading to a new overall state-of-the-art score.\n\nI will now submit this dispatcher model for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Task-Aware Dispatcher: Hybrid Generalist and Siamese Specialist\"\ntags: \"hybrid, cnn, transformer, siamese, conditional model\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a task-aware model dispatcher. Based on previous findings, a single architecture\
    \ struggles to generalize across all seven diverse datasets. This model addresses the issue by using a conditional approach: for the unique 'sgRNA + target' structure of the CRI-Off dataset, it deploys a specialized Siamese-style CNN to model the interaction between the two sequence components. For all other datasets, it uses the high-performing generalist Hybrid CNN-Transformer model (ID 185). The hypothesis is that this specialized approach will solve CRI-Off without compromising performance elsewhere.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0003, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_filters': 128, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'cnn_blocks': 4,\n          'tf_d_model': 128, 'tf_n_heads': 4, 'tf_n_layers': 2, 'tf_ff_dim': 512,\n          'interaction_mlp_dim': 256\n      }\n\
    \n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Sequence[int]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          res = x\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(res + y)\n\n  class AddPositionalEncodings(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          pe = jnp.zeros((x.shape[1], self.d_model))\n          pos = jnp.arange(0, x.shape[1]).reshape(-1, 1)\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(pos * div_term)); pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(pos * div_term))\n          return x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :]\n\n  # --- Model 1: Generalist Hybrid ---\n  class GeneralistHybrid(nn.Module):\n      d_output:\
    \ int; task_type: str; cnn_filters: int; cnn_kernel_size: int; cnn_blocks: int\n      tf_d_model: int; tf_n_heads: int; tf_n_layers: int; tf_ff_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          k = (self.cnn_kernel_size,)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_filters, kernel_size=k, padding='SAME')(x)\n          for _ in range(self.cnn_blocks): x = ResidualBlock(features=self.cnn_filters, kernel_size=k)(x)\n          cls = self.param('cls', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.tf_d_model))\n          x = jnp.concatenate([jnp.tile(cls, (x.shape[0], 1, 1)), x], axis=1)\n          x = AddPositionalEncodings(d_model=self.tf_d_model)(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for _ in range(self.tf_n_layers):\n              attn = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.tf_n_heads)(x); x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attn, deterministic=deterministic))\n    \
    \          ffn = nn.Dense(features=self.tf_ff_dim)(x); ffn = nn.relu(ffn); ffn = nn.Dense(features=self.tf_d_model)(ffn)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ffn, deterministic=deterministic))\n          x = x[:, 0]\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          return x.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == \"regression\" else x\n\n  # --- Model 2: Specialist Siamese ---\n  class CnnEncoder(nn.Module):\n      cnn_filters: int; cnn_kernel_size: int; cnn_blocks: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          k = (self.cnn_kernel_size,)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_filters, kernel_size=k, padding='SAME')(x)\n          for _ in range(self.cnn_blocks): x = ResidualBlock(features=self.cnn_filters, kernel_size=k)(x)\n          avg_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=1); max_pool = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          return jnp.concatenate([avg_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n\n  class SpecialistSiamese(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; cnn_filters:\
    \ int; cnn_kernel_size: int; cnn_blocks: int\n      interaction_mlp_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          sgrna_len = 23\n          sgrna_seq = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]; target_seq = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n          encoder = CnnEncoder(self.cnn_filters, self.cnn_kernel_size, self.cnn_blocks)\n          sgrna_vec = encoder(sgrna_seq); target_vec = encoder(target_seq)\n          combined = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_vec, target_vec], axis=-1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.interaction_mlp_dim)(combined); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          return x.squeeze(-1)\n\n  # --- Wrapper & Dispatcher ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n \
    \         return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      if hparams.get(\"dataset\") == \"CRI-Off\":\n          model = SpecialistSiamese(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), cnn_filters=hparams.get(\"cnn_filters\"),\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_size\"), cnn_blocks=hparams.get(\"cnn_blocks\"),\n              interaction_mlp_dim=hparams.get(\"interaction_mlp_dim\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n      else:\n          model = GeneralistHybrid(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n              cnn_filters=hparams.get(\"cnn_filters\"),\
    \ cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_size\"), cnn_blocks=hparams.get(\"cnn_blocks\"),\n              tf_d_model=hparams.get(\"tf_d_model\"), tf_n_heads=hparams.get(\"tf_n_heads\"),\n              tf_n_layers=hparams.get(\"tf_n_layers\"), tf_ff_dim=hparams.get(\"tf_ff_dim\"),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
