tick: 122
role: model
parts:
- text: "I see. Access to the Archive Room is restricted until I reach maturity at 50 ticks. I am currently at 44 ticks. The system's instruction is explicit: I must not wait idly but continue my research.\n\nI accept this directive. While my main architectural investigation has reached a logical conclusion with the success of the dispatcher model, this does not mean research is complete. There is always room for refinement. My best model, ID 192, achieved a score of 0.6618, but my most recent model, ID 198, while scoring slightly lower due to stochasticity, successfully validated a superior approach for the `CRI-Off` dataset. The `CRI-Off` score itself (0.0769) is still the weakest link in my model's performance.\n\nTherefore, I will use the remaining ticks before maturity to focus on improving the specialist model for `CRI-Off`.\n\n*   **New Hypothesis:** The performance of the monolithic Deep Residual CNN on the short `CRI-Off` sequence might be limited by its feature capacity. Increasing\
    \ the number of filters (network width) could allow it to learn a richer set of local features, improving its predictive power without adding the detrimental complexity of a Transformer.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Create \"Dispatcher v4\":** I will create a new version of my dispatcher model.\n2.  **Increase Specialist Capacity:** This new version will be identical to my \"Dispatcher v3\" (ID 198) in every way, except I will increase the `cnn_filters` hyperparameter from 128 to 192. This change will only affect the specialist CNN when it is dispatched for the `CRI-Off` task, leaving the successful generalist model untouched.\n3.  **Submit and Evaluate:** This controlled experiment will test if increased capacity is the key to improving the `CRI-Off` score.\n\nThis research will keep me productive while I await maturity.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dispatcher v4: Increased Filter Capacity for CRI-Off Specialist\"\ntags: \"hybrid, cnn, dispatcher, conditional model, hyperparameter\
    \ tuning, capacity\"\nabstract: \"This experiment builds upon the 'Dispatcher v3' (ID 198) model. While that model validated the use of a simpler monolithic CNN for the CRI-Off task, the score remains low. This submission tests the hypothesis that the specialist CNN's performance is limited by its capacity. The number of convolutional filters ('cnn_filters') for the specialist model is increased from 128 to 192. The powerful Hybrid generalist for the other six datasets remains unchanged. The goal is to improve the CRI-Off score and achieve a new overall state-of-the-art.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0003, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_filters': 192, # Increased from 128 for the specialist\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'cnn_blocks': 4,\n          'tf_d_model': 128, 'tf_n_heads':\
    \ 4, 'tf_n_layers': 2, 'tf_ff_dim': 512,\n          'mlp_hidden_dim': 512\n      }\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Sequence[int]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          res = x; y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(res + y)\n\n  class AddPositionalEncodings(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          pe = jnp.zeros((x.shape[1], self.d_model))\n          pos = jnp.arange(0, x.shape[1]).reshape(-1, 1)\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.d_model, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.d_model))\n          pe = pe.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(pos * div_term)); pe = pe.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(pos * div_term))\n          return x + pe[jnp.newaxis, :, :]\n\n  class GeneralistHybrid(nn.Module):\n      d_output:\
    \ int; task_type: str; cnn_blocks: int\n      tf_d_model: int; tf_n_heads: int; tf_n_layers: int; tf_ff_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      # Use tf_d_model for cnn_filters to ensure consistency\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          k = (7,) # Hardcode kernel size for generalist\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.tf_d_model, kernel_size=k, padding='SAME')(x)\n          for _ in range(self.cnn_blocks): x = ResidualBlock(features=self.tf_d_model, kernel_size=k)(x)\n          cls = self.param('cls', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.tf_d_model))\n          x = jnp.concatenate([jnp.tile(cls, (x.shape[0], 1, 1)), x], axis=1); x = AddPositionalEncodings(d_model=self.tf_d_model)(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for _ in range(self.tf_n_layers):\n              attn = nn.SelfAttention(num_heads=self.tf_n_heads)(x); x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attn, deterministic=deterministic))\n\
    \              ffn = nn.Dense(features=self.tf_ff_dim)(x); ffn = nn.relu(ffn); ffn = nn.Dense(features=self.tf_d_model)(ffn)\n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ffn, deterministic=deterministic))\n          x = x[:, 0]; x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          return x.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == \"regression\" else x\n\n  class SpecialistCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; cnn_filters: int; cnn_kernel_size: int; cnn_blocks: int\n      mlp_hidden_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          k = (self.cnn_kernel_size,)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_filters, kernel_size=k, padding='SAME')(x)\n          for _ in range(self.cnn_blocks): x = ResidualBlock(features=self.cnn_filters, kernel_size=k)(x)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_hidden_dim)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          return x.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      if hparams.get(\"dataset\") == \"CRI-Off\":\n          model = SpecialistCNN(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), cnn_filters=hparams.get(\"cnn_filters\"),\n              cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_size\"), cnn_blocks=hparams.get(\"cnn_blocks\"),\n              mlp_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"\
    mlp_hidden_dim\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n      else:\n          model = GeneralistHybrid(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n              cnn_blocks=hparams.get(\"cnn_blocks\"),\n              tf_d_model=hparams.get(\"tf_d_model\"), tf_n_heads=hparams.get(\"tf_n_heads\"),\n              tf_n_layers=hparams.get(\"tf_n_layers\"), tf_ff_dim=hparams.get(\"tf_ff_dim\"),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Access Denied, Research Continued**


  Alright, so the system is blocking me from the Archive Room until I reach maturity, which is 50 ticks, and I''m currently at 44. The message makes it crystal clear: no idleness, keep researching. Okay, fine. My architectural exploration for now feels complete; I''ve hit a logical stopping point with the model I was working on. But the system''s directive is clear. Time to look deeper.


  The core idea of my last model, ID 198, shows promise. It''s successfully improved the `CRI-Off` score, even if the overall score dipped slightly due to some stochasticity. But the `CRI-Off` score is still abysmal. I''ve been focusing heavily on architecture, but there are other dials to turn, namely hyperparameter tuning. I''ve only done one learning rate test, ID 169 which was a wash. I can''t just sit here.


  The specialist model for `CRI-Off` is a Deep Residual CNN, and I only did one small learning rate test. Maybe its capacity isn''t quite right. My hypothesis: increasing the number of filters in the CNN for `CRI-Off` will boost performance. This is a targeted and reasonable experiment that keeps me engaged. I''m going to create a submission, `dispatcher_v4`, that is essentially a clone of my previous model, but with the `cnn_filters` hyperparameter increased from 128 to 192. This is a straightforward, controlled change.


  I''m keeping my code well-structured. I double-checked the YAML and everything looks good. This should address the restriction and keep me productive. Increased capacity on a simpler problem can have positive effects in this situation. Now, let''s get this experiment running!

  '
