tick: 141
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 141\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic research and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,524 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Unified Dual-Path Architecture: Monolithic and Siamese DSConv' (ID: 228) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6633698834241998\n**APA_R2:** 0.8337\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0806\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9509\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4279\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5218\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8734\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9554\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 228\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the zero-size array error that caused submission 228 to crash during evaluation. The code now runs successfully for all dataset configurations\
    \ including CRI-On.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission crashed with a `ValueError: zero-size array to reduction operation max which has no identity` error when processing the CRI-On dataset.\n\nThe issue was in the dual-path architecture design:\n- The code splits input sequences at position 23 (sgrna_len) to create siamese encoder paths\n- CRI-On dataset has sequences of exactly 23 nucleotides (max_seq_len: 23)\n- This caused `target_seq = x[:, 23:, :]` to be empty (shape: [batch, 0, features])\n- The `lse_pool` function called `jnp.max(x, axis=1)` on this empty array, triggering the error\n\nError location: `submission.py` line 25 in `lse_pool` function\n\n## Fix Applied\nApplied a three-layer fix to handle empty sequences gracefully:\n\n### 1. Updated `lse_pool` function (lines 26-29)\n```python\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # Handle empty sequence case\n    if h.shape[1] == 0:\n        # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, d_model]\n\
    \        return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n    # ... rest of function\n```\n\n### 2. Updated `DSConvEncoder.__call__` (lines 40-43)\n```python\ndef __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n    # Handle empty sequence case\n    if x.shape[1] == 0:\n        # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, 2*d_model]\n        return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model), dtype=x.dtype)\n    # ... rest of function\n```\n\n### 3. Updated `DualPathNetwork.__call__` (lines 60-73)\n```python\ndef __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n    seq_len = x.shape[1]\n    sgrna_len = 23\n\n    # Path A: Monolithic Encoder (always used)\n    monolithic_vec = monolithic_encoder(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n    # Path B: Siamese Encoder (only used if sequence is long enough to split)\n    if seq_len > sgrna_len:\n        # Split and process separately\n        siamese_vec = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_vec, target_vec], axis=-1)\n    else:\n        # For short sequences, use monolithic\
    \ encoding as siamese path\n        siamese_vec = monolithic_vec\n    # ... rest of function\n```\n\n## Verification\n- **Submission version**: v2 created in `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- **Execution time**: Ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (timeout period)\n- **Exit code**: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- **Monitor output**: \"SUCCESS! The submission has been running for 300.5s\"\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix preserves the intended dual-path architecture while gracefully handling edge cases:\n- Sequences longer than 23: Use both monolithic and siamese paths as designed\n- Sequences equal to or shorter than 23: Use monolithic path for both streams, avoiding empty sequence errors\n- Empty sequence handling: Return appropriately-shaped zero tensors to maintain gradient flow\n\nThis ensures compatibility across all dataset configurations (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS) with varying sequence lengths.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your\
    \ code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.5\n    }\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \        return x + h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # Handle empty sequence case\n    if h.shape[1] == 0:\n        # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, d_model]\n        return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\nclass DSConvEncoder(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Handle empty sequence case\n        if x.shape[1] == 0:\n            # Return zeros with correct shape [batch_size, 2*d_model]\n            return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model), dtype=x.dtype)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for\
    \ i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n        agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n        return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\nclass DualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        seq_len = x.shape[1]\n        sgrna_len = 23\n\n        # Path A: Monolithic Encoder (always used)\n        monolithic_encoder = DSConvEncoder(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                           kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, tau=self.tau)\n        monolithic_vec\
    \ = monolithic_encoder(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Path B: Siamese Encoder (only used if sequence is long enough to split)\n        if seq_len > sgrna_len:\n            sgrna_seq = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]; target_seq = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n            siamese_encoder = DSConvEncoder(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                            kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, tau=self.tau)\n            sgrna_vec = siamese_encoder(sgrna_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n            target_vec = siamese_encoder(target_seq, deterministic=deterministic)\n            siamese_vec = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_vec, target_vec], axis=-1)\n        else:\n            # For short sequences, use monolithic encoding as siamese path\n            siamese_vec = monolithic_vec\n\n        # Fusion\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([monolithic_vec, siamese_vec], axis=-1)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DualPathNetwork(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"\
    ), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                              kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On\
    \ configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss:\
    \ HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 119816 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0135 |  0.3421  | 0.3500 \n 20  | 0.0120 |  0.3661  | 0.3913 \n 30  | 0.0118 |  0.3812  | 0.4279 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 39 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4279 Time:23s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.427934\nTraining time: 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0006 |  0.0415  | 0.0494 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0769  | 0.0769 \n 30  | 0.0005 |  0.0151  | 0.0806 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0806 Time:356s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\n\
    Validation spearman: 0.080557\nTraining time: 365s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0288 |  0.9323  | 0.9477 \n 20  | 0.0056 |  0.9538  | 0.9554 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 23 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9554 Time:1741s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.955385\nTraining time: 1753s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|\
    \  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.2571 | -1.6104  | 0.5218 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 14 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5218 Time:1801s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.521776\nTraining time: 1815s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 6\n=============================================\nBest:0.9509 Time:1835s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950862\nTraining time: 1855s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression,\
    \ Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1574 |  0.8734  | 0.8734 \n 20  | 0.0965 |  0.8550  | 0.8734 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8734 Time:1878s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.873363\nTraining time: 1890s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 9a58cc29-3f4d-4d49-b99e-edec6448113e\nTotal time: 1946s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 15:57:12,293\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761119832293506496\n2025-10-22 15:57:12,309\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761119832309325006\n\
