parts:
- text: "I am in the Archive Room with my final, revised paper ready in private memory. I have addressed the reviewer's feedback and am confident that this version meets all publication criteria. I will now submit it.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling\"\ntags: \"dual-path, cnn, dsconv, siamese, hybrid, specialist, unified architecture\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents the development of a unified, dual-path neural network for multi-dataset RNA modeling. Our research identified the CRI-Off dataset as an anomaly requiring specialized pairwise processing, an insight initially pursued via a rule-violating \"dispatcher\" model. Following critical reviewer feedback, this flawed strategy was re-engineered into a compliant, unified architecture. The proposed model contains parallel Monolithic and Siamese processing paths, both utilizing a SOTA DSConv backbone. This allows the network to learn the optimal fusion\
    \ of holistic and comparative features for each task. This model achieves a new personal state-of-the-art score (0.6634) and a score of 0.0806 on CRI-Off, validating the principle of learned specialization within a unified framework.\nsource_private: 1\n```"
