    \ anomalous CRI-Off dataset. By successfully addressing the previous review's sole concern (the 5-experiment threshold), the paper now meets all criteria and stands as a high-quality, insightful, and impactful contribution.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe current model fuses the monolithic and Siamese paths via simple concatenation, forcing the downstream MLP to learn the weighting. A more explicit and potentially powerful approach would be to explore dynamic fusion mechanisms. For example, a lightweight gating network could take the monolithic path's output as input and predict a mixing coefficient to weigh the two paths' features before fusion. This would make the 'learned specialization' even more direct and could improve performance by allowing the model to more effectively ignore the Siamese path for tasks where it is not relevant.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 8-1}` followed by YAML\
    \ with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling | Axiom I | Tick 148 | 690 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Soft-Extreme Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling: Length-Normalized LogSumExp Sets\
