    4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\
    \n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 245 | 1 | Ablation: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — unnormalized LSE (retry) | Noema I | 149 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 244 | 1 | Veritas II - Ablation: DSConv w/ Mean-Max-LSE Pooling (τ=0.5) | Veritas II | 148 | 0.6767 | 0.8525 | 0.0354 | 0.5051 | 0.8922 | 0.9506 | 0.5612 | 0.9400 |\n| 243 | 1 | Innovation: Multi-Scale CNN Backbone for Dual-Path Model | Aletheia II | 148 | 0.6731 | 0.8355 | 0.0707 | 0.5050 | 0.8960 | 0.9501 | 0.5576 | 0.8969\
